  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">APF - Asia Pacific Forum on National Human Rights Institutions 2016-2018 - APF - Asia Pacific Forum of National Human Rights</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Asia Pacific Forum of NHRI&apos;s 2016-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia Pacific Forum is a regional network of national human rights institutions from 25 countries in the Asia Pacific region. The Swedish support has been provided as un-earmarked support to the implementation of APF Strategic Plan 2015-2020.&#xa0;
The strategic plan builds on a theory of change:&#xa0;
The APF&#x2019;s theory of change asserts that independent and effective NHRIs, acting individually and collectively to: influence laws, policies, practices and attitudes, will create an improved human rights environment in the Asia Pacific.
The Strategic Plan identified the following strategic human rights priorities:
In pursuing its functions from 2015 to 2020 the APF will foster human rights, peace and security by addressing civil, political, economic, social and cultural rights with priority accorded to the following groups:
Children; Women; People with disabilities; Mass movement of people (including asylum seekers, refugees, migrants, internally and externally displaced persons); and Older persons.
In addition to the above, the APF will also prioritize activities relating to business and human rights.
APF has identified the following outcomes of its support to National Human Rights Institutions:
Outcome 1: Increased number of NHRIs complying with UN and international standards.
Outcome 2: NHRIs are better able to perform their functions in the areas of complaints, education, monitoring, advocacy and reporting.
Outcome 3: A more conducive environment for the recognition of NHRIs at the national, regional and international level.
Outcome 4: APF is well-governed, sustainably resourced, strategically directed and member-owned.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;det skall utg&#xe5; till den regionala organisationen Asia Pacific Forum for National Human Rights Institutions (APF). APF &#xe4;r ett medlemsbaserat n&#xe4;tverk av nationella institutioner f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos dessa institutioner f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja, skydda och &#xf6;vervaka efterlevnaden av FN:s internationella konventioner f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support will go to the regional organization Asia Pacific Forum for National Human Rights Institutions (APF). APF is a member-based network of national human rights institutions aimed at strengthening the capacity of these institutions to promote, protect and monitor compliance with UN international human rights conventions.</narrative>
  </description>
